          "type": "inline_review_comment",
          "author": "gemini-code-assist[bot]",
          "path": "common/src/test/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/common/cache/AnalyticsCacheCaffeineImplTest.java",
          "line": 108,
          "diff_hunk": "Impl<String, String> ttlCache =\n+        AnalyticsCacheCaffeineImpl.createWithTtlOnly(1, TimeUnit.NANOSECONDS);\n+\n+    ttlCache.put(\"key1\", \"value1\");\n+    long start = System.nanoTime();\n+    while (System.nanoTime() - start < 1_000L) {\n+      Thread.onSpinWait();\n+    }\n+    ttlCache.cleanUp();\n+\n+    assertThat(ttlCache.get(\"key1\")).isEmpty();\n+    assertThat(ttlCache.size()).isEqualTo(0);\n+  }",
          "body": "![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)\n\nBusy-waiting using a spin loop (`Thread.onSpinWait()`) with a very short duration (1,000 nanoseconds) is highly prone to flakiness in virtualized CI/CD environments due to CPU scheduling, GC pauses, and coarse system timer resolutions.\n\nUsing `TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS` with a short `Thread.sleep(10)` is much more robust, consumes no CPU while waiting, and ensures the entry has expired across all platforms.\n\n```java\n  void createWithTtlOnly_expiredEntry_evictsOnCleanUp() throws InterruptedException {\n    AnalyticsCacheCaffeineImpl<String, String> ttlCache =\n        AnalyticsCacheCaffeineImpl.createWithTtlOnly(1, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);\n\n    ttlCache.put(\"key1\", \"value1\");\n    Thread.sleep(10);\n    ttlCache.cleanUp();\n\n    assertThat(ttlCache.get(\"key1\")).isEmpty();\n    assertThat(ttlCache.size()).isEqualTo(0);\n  }\n```",
          "created_at": "2026-10-29T10:14:09Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gcs-analytics-core/pull/441#discussion_r4411085673"
        }
      ]
